WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.752
The fame versus uniqueness grid audits your brand assets.

00:00:03.802 --> 00:00:05.273
Each one lands in a box:

00:00:05.323 --> 00:00:06.358
use or lose,

00:00:06.408 --> 00:00:07.596
avoid solo use,

00:00:07.646 --> 00:00:08.693
invest potential,

00:00:08.743 --> 00:00:10.138
or ignore.

00:00:10.833 --> 00:00:14.568
A shopper hears just Have a break, and instantly thinks KitKat.

00:00:14.618 --> 00:00:16.231
Famous and unique.

00:00:16.281 --> 00:00:18.263
Use it or lose it.

00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:20.922
But a plain blue bank billboard?

00:00:20.972 --> 00:00:22.915
People guess three different banks.

00:00:22.965 --> 00:00:25.308
Famous, but shared by rivals.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.693
Invest potential at best.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.848
So list every asset,

00:00:29.898 --> 00:00:30.698
place each one on the grid,

00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:32.159
then protect it,

00:00:32.209 --> 00:00:33.009
build it,

00:00:32.787 --> 00:00:34.502
or drop it.
